      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hepatic blood flow was monitored in cats during myocardial ischemia (MI). Increased plasma CPK activity, the S-T segment of the electrocardiogram, and hepatic flow was reduced by 5 h to 40% of control. The results suggest that MI can influence organs distant from the original ischemic episode."},
